Respondent Tol Wassman hereby applies for the Court to issue an order restraining Petitioner Lexi Mattick from disseminating the proprietary source code and trade secrets related to Respondent's software platform, TormentNexus.

This application is made pursuant to California Code of Civil Procedure section 527 on the grounds that great and irreparable injury will result to Respondent before the matter can be heard on regular notice. #continuation

Specifically, Petitioner has communicated an explicit intent to publicly share a copy of the TormentNexus source code. This would destroy the trade secret status of Respondent's software, inflicting severe damage with no adequate remedy.

This application is based on the Memorandum of Points and Authorities, the Declaration of Johnny Appleseed, all records on file, and any further arguments and evidence that may be presented to the Court.

